setup-title = Show what your agents are doing
setup-intro = Folder Tree learns what Claude Code and Codex do from small hooks that leave empty marker files in a .foldertree folder (kept out of git). It only reads their names. In the folder you copied Folder Tree to, run:
setup-claude = Claude Code: two hooks are added to ~/.claude/settings.json and work from its next session. Updated Folder Tree? Run the command again.
setup-codex = Codex: the same two hooks are added to ~/.codex/hooks.json; Codex asks you to trust them once.
setup-other = Other agents: run node hooks/watch.mjs --pane "name" in the project to mark files as they change. To take the hooks out again, add --remove.
